cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use turncoat-sdn in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "turncoat-sdn: a reproducible benchmark for trust-aware SDN load balancers under delayed-onset attacks"
abstract: >-
  turncoat-sdn is a benchmark for trust-aware load balancers in
  software-defined edge networks under delayed-onset ("turncoat") attacks:
  servers and IoT devices that behave honestly until an onset, then lie about
  their load, drop tasks, alternate between honest and hostile phases, or
  spoof another device's identity. It provides a seeded discrete-event
  simulator, five load-balancing strategies including a zero-trust EdgeScore
  selector, an attack library with configurable onsets, a versioned event
  recording format with a validator, ground-truth scorers, paired statistics
  with bootstrap confidence intervals and Holm-corrected Wilcoxon tests, and
  an optional live testbed on Mininet that records the same format.
type: software
